<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Android platform auto-backup rules (API 23-30; see data_extraction_rules.xml
  for API 31+). Attached via android:fullBackupContent on <application>.

  Decision: an EXCLUSION list, not android:allowBackup="false".
  Turna's own backup story is the WebDAV channel (see
  lib/service/remote_backup/), which the project deliberately keeps local and
  sanitised. Silencing the platform channel outright would also take away
  "new phone keeps my review history" for users who never configured WebDAV,
  so the platform backup stays and only the sensitive artifact is removed.

  What is excluded: the transparency log. `core/log_capture.dart` writes
  `transparency_log*.jsonl` into `getApplicationDocumentsDirectory()`, which
  on Android is `<dataDir>/app_flutter/` — inside the auto-backup tree. The
  log is the one file the app actively encourages users to share (diagnostic
  export), so leaving it in a cloud backup contradicts the promise the
  privacy page makes. Credentials are not in play: the AI key and the WebDAV
  password live in Keystore-backed secure storage, which the platform never
  backs up.

  What is deliberately NOT excluded, because excluding it would break the
  user's data rather than protect it:
    - `app_flutter/course.db` and `course.db.v<N>.bak` — the learning
      database and its pre-migration snapshots. The downgrade path wipes SRS
      history, so a .bak may be the only copy of that history.
    - `app_flutter/anki_media/` — deck media. The database references it by
      path, so a backup without it restores cards whose images and audio are
      all dead links.
    - the `sharedpref` domain — settings, minus the credentials that
      `SecureCredentialStore` already moved out of prefs.

  NOTE: `domain="root"` is required, not `file`. The documents directory is
  `<dataDir>/app_flutter/`, a sibling of `files/`, so the `file` domain
  (which maps to getFilesDir()) would not match it. Android backup rules
  support no wildcards, so the three concrete file names are listed: the
  active log plus the two rotation files (LogCapture._maxRotatedFiles = 2).
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="root" path="app_flutter/transparency_log.jsonl" />
    <exclude domain="root" path="app_flutter/transparency_log.1.jsonl" />
    <exclude domain="root" path="app_flutter/transparency_log.2.jsonl" />
</full-backup-content>
